<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis IX, Duke of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1417–1479</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Louis the Rich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis IX, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria-landshut">Bavaria-Landshut</a>, called the Rich, ruled from 1450 to 1479. Like his father Henry XVI and his son George, he drew great wealth from his well-managed duchy. He expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> from his lands in 1450, founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-ingolstadt">University of Ingolstadt</a> in 1472, and his son's wedding in 1475 is still re-enacted as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landshut">Landshut</a> Wedding.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-ix-duke-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Louis IX, Duke of Bavaria" width="320" height="518" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gliwi · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amalia_von_Sachsen_und_Ludwig_IX._(Bayern).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
